  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nIn Book.sol, the function [addOrderToBook()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/types/Book.sol#L150) is called to add limit orders to the book. This function calls two other functions, _updateBookPostOrder and _updateLimitPostOrder\n\n```solidity\n /// @dev Adds a limit order to the book\n    function addOrderToBook(Book storage self, Order memory order) internal {\n        Limit storage limit = _updateBookPostOrder(self, order);\n\n        _updateLimitPostOrder(self, limit, order);\n    }\n```\nIn [_updateBookPostOrder](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/types/Book.sol#L256-L270), the price is added to the tree, the book's metadata is updated, and the order is added to storage.\n```solidity\n    function _updateBookPostOrder(Book storage self, Order memory order) private returns (Limit storage limit) {\n        if (order.side == Side.BUY) {\n            limit = self.bidLimits[order.price];\n            if (limit.numOrders == 0) self.bidTree.insert(order.price);\n            self.metadata().numBids++;\n            self.metadata().quoteTokenOpenInterest += self.getQuoteTokenAmount(order.price, order.amount);\n        } else {\n            limit = self.askLimits[order.price];\n            if (limit.numOrders == 0) self.askTree.insert(order.price);\n            self.metadata().numAsks++;\n            self.metadata().baseTokenOpenInterest += order.amount;\n        }\n\n\n        self.orders[order.id] = order;\n    }\n```\nIn [_updateLimitPostOrder](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/92a8839e3eb9715d53e24f0168442cecdc9b784b/contracts/clob/types/Book.sol#L281), the limit for the price is updated, adding the new order and updating the previous and next order id to ensure orderliness of the orders.\n```solidity\n    function _updateLimitPostOrder(Book storage self, Limit storage limit, Order memory order) private {\n        limit.numOrders++;\n\n\n        if (limit.headOrder.isNull()) {\n            limit.headOrder = order.id;\n            limit.tailOrder = order.id;\n        } else {\n            Order storage tailOrder = self.orders[limit.tailOrder];\n            tailOrder.nextOrderId = order.id;\n            order.prevOrderId = tailOrder.id;\n            limit.tailOrder = order.id;\n        }\n\n\n```\nThe `issue` here is that after the `order` has already been added to storage in _updateBookPostOrder.\n```solidity\n function _updateBookPostOrder(Book storage self, Order memory order) private returns (Limit storage limit) {\n         ...\n        self.orders[order.id] = order;\n    }\n\n```\n_updateLimitPostOrder is called, and the order passed into _updateLimitPostOrder is of type `memory`, therefore, when the `prevOrderId` for the new order is updated, this only happens to the order passed in and not the one in storage.\n```solidity\n function _updateLimitPostOrder(Book storage self, Limit storage limit, Order memory order) private {\n  ....\n        } else {\n            Order storage tailOrder = self.orders[limit.tailOrder];\n            tailOrder.nextOrderId = order.id;\n   @>       order.prevOrderId = tailOrder.id; //@audit this memory \n            limit.tailOrder = order.id;\n        ....\n    }\n\n```\nIn solidity, once a value in `memory` is saved to `storage`, any further changes to that memory value do `not` reflect in storage. The value in storage stays the same as when it was first stored.\n\n## impact\n\nThis means all the orders added to the book do not have their `prevOrderId` saved with them.\nThis will severely disrupt the orderliness of the book, leading to orders becoming lost in the book and can never be filled. \n\nWhen, for any reason, an order is removed, it is assumed to be the head and the next order is made the new head of the orders in the price limit.\n```solidity\n    function _updateLimitRemoveOrder(Book storage self, Order storage order) private {\n        uint256 price = order.price;\n .....\n\n        limit.numOrders--;\n\n        OrderId prev = order.prevOrderId;\n        OrderId next = order.nextOrderId;\n\n@>      if (!prev.isNull()) self.orders[prev].nextOrderId = next;\n        else limit.headOrder = next;\n\n        if (!next.isNull()) self.orders[next].prevOrderId = prev;\n        else limit.tailOrder = prev;\n    }\n}\n```\nExample, lets say there are ten order in a particular limit, then the seventh order is removed, since its `prevOrderId` does not exist (is null) the function `_updateLimitRemoveOrder` will treat it as the first order in the price limit and set its next id as the new head of the limit, leaving the first six orders lost and unable to be fulfilled.\n\n\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nSet the previous id of the new order before adding it to storage in `_updateBookPostOrder` or pass in its storage version in _updateLimitPostOrder so any changes to the new order will reflect in storage.\n```diff\n-- function _updateLimitPostOrder(Book storage self, Limit storage limit, Order memory order) private {\n++ function _updateLimitPostOrder(Book storage self, Limit storage limit, Order storage order) private {\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {Order} from \"contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\nimport {CLOB} from \"contracts/clob/CLOB.sol\";\nimport {Side} from \"contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\nimport {Limit} from \"contracts/clob/types/Book.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        // Setup\n        address user = users[0];\n        uint256 amountInBase = 2 ether;\n        uint256 price = 100 ether;\n\n        // will create a 7 limit orders, check that all thier prevOrderId is equal to 0\n\n        setupTokens(Side.SELL, user, amountInBase * 7, price, true);\n\n        // Prepare arguments\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: amountInBase,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            price: price,\n            cancelTimestamp: NEVER,\n            side: Side.SELL,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        });\n\n\n        // run a loop seven times to create 7 limit orders\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < 7; i++) {\n            // Expect events\n            vm.expectEmit(true, true, true, true);\n            emit CLOB.LimitOrderSubmitted(clob.getEventNonce() + 1, user, i + 1, args);\n\n            vm.expectEmit(true, true, true, true);\n            emit CLOB.LimitOrderProcessed(clob.getEventNonce() + 3, user, i + 1, amountInBase, int256(0), -int256(0), 0);\n\n            // Post limit order\n            vm.startPrank(user);\n            ICLOB.PostLimitOrderResult memory result = clob.postLimitOrder(user, args);\n            vm.stopPrank();\n\n            // Verify results\n            assertEq(result.orderId, i + 1, \"Order ID should match\");\n            assertEq(result.amountPostedInBase, amountInBase, \"Remaining amount should match\");\n            assertEq(result.quoteTokenAmountTraded, int256(0), \"Quote token change should be zero\");\n            assertEq(result.baseTokenAmountTraded, -int256(0), \"Base token change should be zero\");\n\n            // Check order book state and that all thier prevOrderId is equal to 0\n            Order memory order = clob.getOrder(i + 1);\n            assertEq(order.owner, user, \"Order owner should match\");\n            assertEq(order.amount, amountInBase, \"Order amount should match\");\n            assertEq(order.price, price, \"Order price should match\");\n            \n            //this show that the prevOrderId is never set when the order is added and is always zero\n            assertEq(order.prevOrderId.unwrap(), 0, \"Previous order ID should be zero\");\n\n        }\n\n        // then remove the 5th order and check that the limit head now is set to the 6th order\n       uint256 [] memory orderIdToRemove = new uint256[](1);\n        orderIdToRemove[0] = 5;\n\n        // Pass it into the struct properly\n        ICLOB.CancelArgs memory cancelArgs = ICLOB.CancelArgs({\n            orderIds: orderIdToRemove\n        });\n        // remove the 5th order\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        clob.cancel(user, cancelArgs);\n        vm.stopPrank(); \n\n        // Verify that the order was removed\n        Order memory removedOrder = clob.getOrder(orderIdToRemove[0]); \n        assertEq(removedOrder.id.unwrap(), 0, \"Removed order should not exist\");\n\n        // Verify that the head of the limit order book under the same price is now the 6th order\n        // showing that the first fours orders are lost in the orderbook and never be fulfilled\n        Limit memory newLimit = clob.getLimit(price, Side.SELL);\n        assertEq(newLimit.headOrder.unwrap(), 6, \"New head order should be the 6th order after removal\");\n       \n\n       \n    }\n\n}\n\n```",
